# Line endings. Every tracked file in this repository is LF today and none
# carries a CR (checked before this file was written), so this pins what is
# already true rather than changing anything. It matters because dev/wsl2.md
# invites contributions from Windows, where a checkout would otherwise arrive
# as CRLF and every diff would be the whole file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fuzz corpora are fixtures whose exact bytes ARE the test. An entry rewritten
# by a checkout is a different input from the one that found the bug, which is
# the one thing a regression corpus must never be. 2,084 of them.
**/testdata/fuzz/** -text

# The hostile-input corpus, for the same reason: its whole purpose is bytes a
# guest chose, including ones a normaliser would have opinions about.
testdata/hostile/** -text

# Binary artefacts.
*.gif   binary
*.png   binary
*.ext4  binary
*.img   binary

# Generated by `make docs`, not written by hand — CI fails on drift between
# these and the source they come from. Marking them keeps a 786 KB regenerated
# file out of the language statistics and collapses it in review, where it is
# noise rather than a change somebody made.
llms.txt          linguist-generated=true
llms-full.txt     linguist-generated=true
docs/reference/** linguist-generated=true

# The decision logs are long-form engineering record rather than product
# documentation; marking them keeps 277 KB of prose out of the language
# statistics and collapses them in review.
docs/decisions.md          linguist-documentation=true
docs/decisions-features.md linguist-documentation=true
docs/roadmap.md            linguist-documentation=true
